 defeat the  disease we need what's called herd  immunity and the best way to get that is  through vaccines if we don't develop  vaccines experts currently estimate that  between 50 and 70 percent of us would  have to get kovat 19 before herd  immunity kicked in and stopped the  pandemic naturally but along the way it  could potentially kill millions of  people so a vaccine offers a safe  alternative to achieving immunity in a  large percentage of the population an  ounce of prevention is really worth a  pound of cure that's why although  treatments are very important long term  vaccines are even more so  a range of potential drugs that might  one day help treat kovat 19 are being  trialed around the world but we don't  really have many results for any of them  so far the World Health Organization is  looking at three candidates in  particular that have shown some promise  first its examining the effects of  established anti malarial drugs on  coronavirus symptoms  waho sponsor trials are also ongoing for  combinations of antivirals that have  already been approved for treating HIV  and finally one of the most promising  substances as a compound called REM des  aveer it was originally developed as a  potential treatment for Ebola but it  didn't work out for that disease as well  as hoped  retrospective testing however showed  that it did affect replication in the  SARS virus so hopes are high that it  might also affect that pathogens close  relative the new corona virus the best  thing about all of these candidates is  that most or all of the development has  already been done for them so production  could be ramped up quickly if they did  prove effective in these clinical trials  we should know soon if any of them work  and before we let you go we step away  from the sobering world of tests and  vaccines to indulge in lighter fare one  restaurant in Hanoi has created the  corona burger so far only available in  Vietnam but it looks set to take off  worldwide it's a beef burger in a green  tea stained virus shaped button the  restaurant owner is delighted with his  creation he says business is good and  they'll hopefully remind customers to  wash their hands before eating  and there are Swiss confectioner's  reminding us of the season but also of  the times when chocolate Easter bunnies  are decorated with little face masks


